{"task_id": "Mbpp/61", "solution": "def count_Substrings(input_string: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the number of substrings in the input_string where the sum of digits\n    equals the substring's length.\n    \"\"\"\n    total_count = 0\n    n = len(input_string)\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        current_sum = 0\n        for j in range(i, n):\n            digit = int(input_string[j])\n            current_sum += digit\n\n            current_length = (j - i) + 1\n\n            if current_sum == current_length:\n                total_count += 1\n\n    return total_count"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/63", "solution": "class NumericalPair:\n    \"\"\"Encapsulates two numerical values and computes their absolute difference.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, val1, val2):\n        self.value1 = val1\n        self.value2 = val2\n\n    def get_absolute_difference(self):\n        \"\"\"Computes and returns the absolute difference between the stored values.\"\"\"\n        return abs(self.value1 - self.value2)\ndef max_difference(tuple_list):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum absolute difference between numerical pairs in a list of tuples.\n    Returns 0 if the input list is empty.\n    \"\"\"\n    max_diff = 0\n    for val1, val2 in tuple_list:\n        pair = NumericalPair(val1, val2)\n        current_diff = pair.get_absolute_difference()\n        if current_diff > max_diff:\n            max_diff = current_diff\n    return max_diff"}
