{"task_id": "Mbpp/74", "solution": "class PatternMapping:\n    \"\"\"\n    Manages and verifies the consistency of one-to-one bidirectional mappings between string elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self):\n        \"\"\"\n        Initializes the mapping dictionaries.\n        \"\"\"\n        self._map1To2 = {}  # Maps elements from the first list to the second\n        self._map2To1 = {}  # Maps elements from the second list to the first\n\n    def isConsistent(self, element1: str, element2: str) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"\n        Checks if a potential mapping between element1 and element2 is consistent with existing mappings.\n        \"\"\"\n        # Check if element1 is already mapped and if its existing mapping matches element2\n        if element1 in self._map1To2:\n            if self._map1To2[element1] != element2:\n                return False\n        \n        # Check if element2 is already mapped and if its existing mapping matches element1\n        if element2 in self._map2To1:\n            if self._map2To1[element2] != element1:\n                return False\n                \n        return True\n\n    def addMapping(self, element1: str, element2: str) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"\n        Attempts to establish a mapping between element1 and element2.\n        Returns True if the mapping is consistent and successfully added/confirmed, False otherwise.\n        \"\"\"\n        # First, check if the proposed mapping is consistent with current rules\n        if not self.isConsistent(element1, element2):\n            return False\n            \n        # If consistent, establish or confirm the bidirectional mapping\n        self._map1To2[element1] = element2\n        self._map2To1[element2] = element1\n        \n        return True\ndef is_samepatterns(list1, list2):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks whether two lists of strings follow the same structural pattern.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Patterns cannot match if the lists have different lengths.\n    if len(list1) != len(list2):\n        return False\n\n    mapper = PatternMapping()\n\n    # Iterate through both lists simultaneously, comparing elements at each position.\n    for i in range(len(list1)):\n        elem1 = list1[i]\n        elem2 = list2[i]\n\n        # Attempt to add the current element pair mapping.\n        # If an inconsistency is detected, the patterns do not match.\n        if not mapper.addMapping(elem1, elem2):\n            return False\n            \n    # If the loop completes, all elements were consistently mapped, so the patterns match.\n    return True"}
