{"task_id": "Mbpp/77", "solution": "def is_Diff(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Determines if a number is divisible by 11 using the alternating sum of digits rule.\"\"\"\n    num_str = str(number)\n    alternating_sum = 0\n    for i, digit_char in enumerate(num_str):\n        digit = int(digit_char)\n        if i % 2 == 0:  # Even index (from right or left, this rule works for either if consistent)\n            alternating_sum += digit\n        else:  # Odd index\n            alternating_sum -= digit\n    \n    # The standard rule is (sum of digits at odd places) - (sum of digits at even places)\n    # The way I've implemented the loop here, for \"12345\":\n    # i=0: alternating_sum += 1  (1)\n    # i=1: alternating_sum -= 2  (-1)\n    # i=2: alternating_sum += 3  (2)\n    # i=3: alternating_sum -= 4  (-2)\n    # i=4: alternating_sum += 5  (3)\n    # This results in: 1 - 2 + 3 - 4 + 5 = 3\n    # This is equivalent to `digit at index 0 - digit at index 1 + digit at index 2 ...`\n    # This sum needs to be divisible by 11.\n    return alternating_sum % 11 == 0"}
