{"task_id": "Mbpp/239", "solution": "def get_total_number_of_sequences(m: int, n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the total number of possible sequences of length n,\n    such that each element is a positive integer and is greater than or equal\n    to twice the previous element but less than or equal to m.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n    if n == 1:\n        return m\n\n    memo = {}\n\n    def _count_sequences_recursive(current_length: int, last_element: int) -> int:\n        if current_length == n:\n            return 1\n\n        if (current_length, last_element) in memo:\n            return memo[(current_length, last_element)]\n\n        count = 0\n        for next_element in range(2 * last_element, m + 1):\n            count += _count_sequences_recursive(current_length + 1, next_element)\n\n        memo[(current_length, last_element)] = count\n        return count\n\n    total_sequences = 0\n    max_first_element = m // (2**(n - 1))\n\n    for first_element in range(1, max_first_element + 1):\n        total_sequences += _count_sequences_recursive(1, first_element)\n\n    return total_sequences"}
