{"task_id": "Mbpp/244", "solution": "import math\ndef next_Perfect_Square(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates and returns the smallest perfect square strictly greater than the input number.\n    It handles negative inputs by finding the next perfect square relative to 0.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Find the integer square root of the number, ensuring it's at least 0.\n    # Add 1 to get the root of the next perfect square.\n    next_root = math.isqrt(max(0, number)) + 1\n    \n    # Square the next root to get the perfect square.\n    return next_root * next_root"}
