{"task_id": "Mbpp/256", "solution": "def count_Primes_nums(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the number of prime numbers strictly less than a given non-negative integer n.\n    It iterates through numbers from 2 to n-1 and checks for primality.\n    \"\"\"\n    def _is_prime(num: int) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"\n        Checks if a given number is prime using trial division up to its square root.\n        This helper function efficiently determines primality.\n        \"\"\"\n        if num < 2:\n            return False\n        if num == 2:\n            return True\n        if num % 2 == 0:\n            return False\n        i = 3\n        while i * i <= num:\n            if num % i == 0:\n                return False\n            i += 2\n        return True\n\n    prime_count = 0\n    for num in range(2, n):\n        if _is_prime(num):\n            prime_count += 1\n    return prime_count"}
