{"task_id": "Mbpp/261", "solution": "def division_elements(tuple1: tuple, tuple2: tuple) -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"\n    Performs element-wise division of two tuples.\n\n    This function performs element-wise mathematical division operation across the given tuples.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(tuple1, tuple) or not isinstance(tuple2, tuple):\n        raise TypeError(\"Both inputs must be tuples.\")\n    if len(tuple1) != len(tuple2):\n        raise ValueError(\"Input tuples must have the same length.\")\n\n    results = []\n    for i in range(len(tuple1)):\n        divisor = tuple2[i]\n        if divisor == 0:\n            raise ZeroDivisionError(\"Cannot divide by zero.\")\n        results.append(tuple1[i] / divisor)\n    return tuple(results)"}
