{"task_id": "Mbpp/283", "solution": "def validate(integer_input: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the frequency of each digit in an integer is less than or equal to the digit's value.\n    Delegates to helper functions for frequency calculation and condition checking.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _calculate_digit_frequencies(number: int) -> dict[int, int]:\n        \"\"\"Calculates the frequency of each digit in the given integer.\"\"\"\n        digit_counts = {}\n        s_number = str(abs(number))\n        for char_digit in s_number:\n            digit = int(char_digit)\n            digit_counts[digit] = digit_counts.get(digit, 0) + 1\n        return digit_counts\n\n    def _check_frequency_condition(digit_frequencies: dict[int, int]) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Verifies if each digit's frequency is less than or equal to its value.\"\"\"\n        for digit, frequency in digit_frequencies.items():\n            if frequency > digit:\n                return False\n        return True\n\n    frequencies = _calculate_digit_frequencies(integer_input)\n    return _check_frequency_condition(frequencies)"}
