{"task_id": "Mbpp/286", "solution": "def max_sub_array_sum_repeated(arr, n, k):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the largest sum of a contiguous subarray in an array conceptually\n    repeated k times, leveraging helper functions for optimal complexity.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _kadane(arr_local):\n        \"\"\"Finds the maximum contiguous subarray sum within a single array.\"\"\"\n        # Handles cases where all numbers are negative correctly.\n        current_max_ending_here = arr_local[0]\n        global_max_so_far = arr_local[0]\n\n        for i in range(1, len(arr_local)):\n            current_max_ending_here = max(arr_local[i], current_max_ending_here + arr_local[i])\n            global_max_so_far = max(global_max_so_far, current_max_ending_here)\n        \n        return global_max_so_far\n\n    def _calculate_total_sum(arr_local):\n        \"\"\"Calculates the sum of all elements in a single array.\"\"\"\n        return sum(arr_local)\n\n    def _calculate_max_prefix_sum(arr_local):\n        \"\"\"Finds the maximum prefix sum of a single array.\"\"\"\n        current_sum = 0\n        max_prefix = float('-inf')\n        for x in arr_local:\n            current_sum += x\n            max_prefix = max(max_prefix, current_sum)\n        return max_prefix\n\n    def _calculate_max_suffix_sum(arr_local):\n        \"\"\"Finds the maximum suffix sum of a single array.\"\"\"\n        current_sum = 0\n        max_suffix = float('-inf')\n        for x in reversed(arr_local):\n            current_sum += x\n            max_suffix = max(max_suffix, current_sum)\n        return max_suffix\n\n    max_sum_single_array = _kadane(arr)\n\n    if k == 1:\n        return max_sum_single_array\n\n    total_sum_arr = _calculate_total_sum(arr)\n    max_prefix_sum = _calculate_max_prefix_sum(arr)\n    max_suffix_sum = _calculate_max_suffix_sum(arr)\n\n    # Initialize final_max_sum with the best sum found within a single array.\n    final_max_sum = max_sum_single_array\n\n    # Case where the maximum subarray spans across the boundary of two array copies (k >= 2).\n    # This involves a suffix from the first array and a prefix from the second.\n    # This is also `max_sum_repeated_case_2` from the design.\n    final_max_sum = max(final_max_sum, max_prefix_sum + max_suffix_sum)\n\n    # Case where the maximum subarray spans multiple array copies (k > 2) and full\n    # middle blocks contribute positively. This is `max_sum_repeated_case_1`.\n    if total_sum_arr > 0 and k > 2:\n        candidate_sum = max_prefix_sum + (k - 2) * total_sum_arr + max_suffix_sum\n        final_max_sum = max(final_max_sum, candidate_sum)\n    \n    # Case where the maximum sum is achieved by taking the entire repeated array,\n    # possible only if the sum of the original array is positive.\n    if total_sum_arr > 0:\n        final_max_sum = max(final_max_sum, total_sum_arr * k)\n\n    return final_max_sum"}
