{"task_id": "Mbpp/395", "solution": "def first_non_repeating_character(s: str) -> str | None:\n    # Tracks character counts and their first occurrence index.\n    # The dictionary insertion order implicitly maintains the first occurrence index for iteration.\n    char_info = {}\n\n    for i, char in enumerate(s):\n        if char not in char_info:\n            char_info[char] = {\"count\": 1, \"first_index\": i}\n        else:\n            char_info[char][\"count\"] += 1\n\n    for char, data in char_info.items():\n        if data[\"count\"] == 1:\n            return char\n\n    return None"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/398", "solution": "def sum_of_digits(numbers_list: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the sum of digits for each number in a list and returns their total sum.\n    \"\"\"\n    total_aggregated_sum = 0\n    for number in numbers_list:\n        current_number_digit_sum = 0\n        # Handle negative numbers by taking absolute value for digit sum\n        abs_number = abs(number)\n        \n        # Handle the case of 0 separately to ensure it adds 0\n        if abs_number == 0:\n            current_number_digit_sum = 0\n        else:\n            while abs_number > 0:\n                current_number_digit_sum += abs_number % 10\n                abs_number //= 10\n        total_aggregated_sum += current_number_digit_sum\n    return total_aggregated_sum"}
