{"task_id": "Mbpp/415", "solution": "def max_Product(arr: list[int]) -> tuple[int, int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds a pair with the highest product from a given array of integers.\n\n    Args:\n        arr: A list of integers.\n\n    Returns:\n        A tuple containing the two integers with the highest product.\n\n    Raises:\n        ValueError: If the input array contains fewer than two elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(arr) < 2:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input array must contain at least two elements.\")\n\n    arr.sort()\n\n    # Product of the two smallest numbers (could be two large negative numbers)\n    product_smallest = arr[0] * arr[1]\n    # Product of the two largest numbers\n    product_largest = arr[-1] * arr[-2]\n\n    if product_smallest > product_largest:\n        return (arr[0], arr[1])\n    else:\n        return (arr[-2], arr[-1])"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/419", "solution": "def round_and_sum(numbers: list[float]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Rounds each number in the input list, sums them, and multiplies by the list's length.\n    Handles an empty input list by returning 0.\n    \"\"\"\n    list_length = len(numbers)\n\n    if not numbers:\n        return 0\n\n    rounded_numbers = [round(num) for num in numbers]\n    sum_rounded = sum(rounded_numbers)\n    final_product = sum_rounded * list_length\n\n    return final_product"}
