{"task_id": "Mbpp/428", "solution": "def shell_sort(arr: list[int]) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts a list of integers in ascending order using the Shell Sort algorithm.\n    It returns a new sorted list, without modifying the original input list.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n    if n <= 1:\n        return list(arr)\n\n    arr_copy = list(arr)\n\n    # Determine initial gap using Knuth's sequence (1, 4, 13, 40, ...)\n    h = 1\n    while h < n // 3:\n        h = 3 * h + 1\n\n    while h >= 1:\n        # Perform a gapped insertion sort for elements at the current gap\n        for i in range(h, n):\n            temp = arr_copy[i]\n            j = i\n            # Shift elements greater than temp to the right by h positions\n            while j >= h and arr_copy[j - h] > temp:\n                arr_copy[j] = arr_copy[j - h]\n                j -= h\n            arr_copy[j] = temp\n        h //= 3 # Decrease the gap\n\n    return arr_copy"}
