{"task_id": "Mbpp/456", "solution": "class String:\n    \"\"\"Encapsulates a single string value and provides the capability to reverse itself.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, value: str):\n        self._value = value\n\n    def reverse(self) -> 'String':\n        \"\"\"Returns a new String object with the characters of the current string reversed.\"\"\"\n        return String(self._value[::-1])\n\n    def get_value(self) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Returns the raw string value.\"\"\"\n        return self._value\nclass StringList:\n    \"\"\"Manages a list of String objects and orchestrates the reversal of each contained string.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, values: list[str]):\n        self._values = [String(v) for v in values]\n\n    def reverse_strings(self) -> 'StringList':\n        \"\"\"Returns a new StringList object where each contained String has been reversed.\"\"\"\n        reversed_internal_strings = [s.reverse() for s in self._values]\n        # We need to extract the raw values for the constructor of the new StringList\n        raw_reversed_values = [s.get_value() for s in reversed_internal_strings]\n        return StringList(raw_reversed_values)\n\n    def get_raw_values(self) -> list[str]:\n        \"\"\"Returns the list of raw string values from the contained String objects.\"\"\"\n        return [s.get_value() for s in self._values]\ndef reverse_string_list(input_list: list[str]) -> list[str]:\n    \"\"\"Reverses each string in a given list of string values.\"\"\"\n    string_list_obj = StringList(input_list)\n    reversed_string_list_obj = string_list_obj.reverse_strings()\n    return reversed_string_list_obj.get_raw_values()"}
