{"task_id": "Mbpp/572", "solution": "def two_unique_nums(numbers: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Identifies numbers that appear exactly once in the input list and returns them\n    in their original relative order of first appearance.\n    \"\"\"\n    number_counts = {}\n    for num in numbers:\n        number_counts[num] = number_counts.get(num, 0) + 1\n\n    unique_numbers = []\n    for num in numbers:\n        if number_counts[num] == 1:\n            unique_numbers.append(num)\n\n    return unique_numbers"}
