{"task_id": "Mbpp/622", "solution": "def get_median(list1: list[float], list2: list[float], size: int) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the median of two sorted lists of the same size.\n\n    Merges the two lists conceptually to find the two middle elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    i = 0  # current index for list1\n    j = 0  # current index for list2\n    \n    m1 = -1  # first middle element\n    m2 = -1  # second middle element\n\n    # The total number of elements is 2 * size.\n    # We need to find the elements at indices (size - 1) and size in the merged list.\n    for count in range(size + 1):\n        if i == size:\n            m1 = m2\n            m2 = list2[j]\n            j += 1\n        elif j == size:\n            m1 = m2\n            m2 = list1[i]\n            i += 1\n        elif list1[i] <= list2[j]:\n            m1 = m2\n            m2 = list1[i]\n            i += 1\n        else:\n            m1 = m2\n            m2 = list2[j]\n            j += 1\n    \n    return (m1 + m2) / 2.0"}
