{"task_id": "Mbpp/630", "solution": "def get_coordinates(coordinate_tuple: tuple) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates all 9 adjacent coordinates (including itself) for a given 2D coordinate,\n    sorts them, and returns them as a list of lists.\n    \"\"\"\n    x, y = coordinate_tuple\n    adjacent_coords = []\n    for dx in [-1, 0, 1]:\n        for dy in [-1, 0, 1]:\n            adjacent_coords.append([x + dx, y + dy])\n\n    # The list is inherently sorted by x then y due to the nested loop order,\n    # but explicitly sorting ensures correctness as per requirements.\n    adjacent_coords.sort(key=lambda coord: (coord[0], coord[1]))\n    return adjacent_coords"}
