{"task_id": "Mbpp/635", "solution": "def heap_sort(data: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Sorts a list of numbers in ascending order using the heap sort algorithm (in-place).\"\"\"\n\n    def _heapify(data: list, n: int, i: int) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Helper function to heapify a subtree rooted with node i.\"\"\"\n        largest = i  # Initialize largest as root\n        left = 2 * i + 1  # left child\n        right = 2 * i + 2  # right child\n\n        # See if left child of root exists and is greater than root\n        if left < n and data[left] > data[largest]:\n            largest = left\n\n        # See if right child of root exists and is greater than current largest\n        if right < n and data[right] > data[largest]:\n            largest = right\n\n        # Change root, if needed\n        if largest != i:\n            data[i], data[largest] = data[largest], data[i]  # swap\n            _heapify(data, n, largest)\n\n    def _build_max_heap(data: list) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Helper function to build a max-heap from the given list.\"\"\"\n        n = len(data)\n        # Build a maxheap.\n        # Since last parent will be at ((n//2)-1) we can start there.\n        for i in range(n // 2 - 1, -1, -1):\n            _heapify(data, n, i)\n\n    n = len(data)\n    if n <= 1:\n        return data\n\n    _build_max_heap(data)\n\n    # One by one extract elements\n    for i in range(n - 1, 0, -1):\n        data[i], data[0] = data[0], data[i]  # swap\n        _heapify(data, i, 0)\n    \n    return data"}
