{"task_id": "Mbpp/743", "solution": "def rotate_right(input_list: list, count: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Rotates a list to the right by a specified number of items.\n    The rotation count is normalized by the list length.\"\"\"\n    n = len(input_list)\n    if n == 0:\n        return []\n\n    effective_count = count % n\n    \n    # Split the list into the part that moves to the front (tail_part)\n    # and the part that remains after it (head_part).\n    tail_part = input_list[n - effective_count:]\n    head_part = input_list[:n - effective_count]\n    \n    return tail_part + head_part"}
