{"task_id": "Mbpp/766", "solution": "def pair_wise(input_list: list) -> list[tuple]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Generates a list of all pairs of consecutive items in a given list.\n    Returns an empty list if input_list has fewer than two elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    result = []\n    # Iterate from the first element up to the second-to-last element\n    for i in range(len(input_list) - 1):\n        # Create a tuple from the current element and the next element\n        result.append((input_list[i], input_list[i+1]))\n    return result"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/763", "solution": "def find_min_diff(arr: tuple, n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the minimum absolute difference between any two elements in the given array.\n    The function sorts the array and then compares adjacent elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n < 2:\n        return 0  # Or handle as an error/specific value depending on requirements for arrays with fewer than 2 elements.\n\n    # Convert tuple to list for sorting\n    sorted_arr = sorted(list(arr))\n\n    min_diff = float('inf')\n\n    # Iterate through the sorted array to find the minimum difference between adjacent elements\n    for i in range(1, n):\n        current_diff = sorted_arr[i] - sorted_arr[i-1]\n        if current_diff < min_diff:\n            min_diff = current_diff\n\n    return min_diff"}
