{"task_id": "Mbpp/791", "solution": "def remove_nested(input_tuple: tuple) -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"\n    Removes nested tuples from the given input_tuple.\n\n    Args:\n        input_tuple: The tuple to process.\n\n    Returns:\n        A new tuple with all nested tuple elements removed,\n        preserving the order of non-tuple elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    result_elements = []\n    for element in input_tuple:\n        if not isinstance(element, tuple):\n            result_elements.append(element)\n    return tuple(result_elements)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/793", "solution": "def last(array: list, element) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the last position of an element in a sorted array.\n    Returns the 0-based index of the last occurrence, or -1 if not found.\n    \"\"\"\n    low = 0\n    high = len(array) - 1\n    result = -1\n\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n        if array[mid] == element:\n            result = mid\n            low = mid + 1\n        elif array[mid] < element:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:  # array[mid] > element\n            high = mid - 1\n    return result"}
